<title>USA: Lockheed Martin says consortium wins deal.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin says consortium wins deal.</headline>
<dateline>GAITHERSBURG, Md. 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Corp. said Friday that a consortium it is involved in has been awarded a $1.55 billion, 10-year contract to provide an advanced national fixed telecommunications network for Britain's armed forces.</p>
<p>The consortium is led by British Telecommunications and includes Lockheed, GEC Marconi Secure Systems and GPT Strategic Communications Systems.</p>
<p>Lockheed Martin said its take of the contract, which was awarded by the British Ministry of Defence, is worth about $100 million over the 10 years of the contract.</p>
<p>Under the deal, the consortium will deliver voice, data and other wide-area networking services for the Royal Navy, Air Force and Army.</p>
</text>
